title: 'statement-store: send a statement that has no routing target on a detour'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On the v2 DHT path a node no longer loses a statement that it cannot route. When the node is
    no replica for the statement's topics and has no connected peer closer to them, it sends the
    statement to its farthest connected full peer, whose own routing peers lie elsewhere in the
    key space. While no peer can take the statement, it stays held in the store, and the
    initial sync of the next routing target delivers it. Before, the retention sweep removed
    such a statement and banned its hash, so a restart of the only routing peer toward a topic
    lost every statement sent in that window.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
